<title>USA: USDA sets interest rates on new commodity loans.</title>
<headline>USDA sets interest rates on new commodity loans.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Monday that interest rates on commodity loans made during December would be 6.5 percent for 1996 crops and 5.5 percent for prior-year crop loans.</p>
<p>In November, the rate was 6.625 percent for new-crop commodity loans and 5.625 percent for 1995 and earlier-year commodities.</p>
<p>USDA rates reflect interest charged by the Treasury for funds. Under the 1996 farm policy law, USDA is required to set its rates one percentage point higher than in the past. The new formula applies to 1996 crops and following years.</p>
</text>
